and the rest of the week,
you've got nothing else.

00:09:16.413 --> 00:09:17.563
You're busy with the rest of your life.

00:09:17.563 --> 00:09:18.889
You're not going to get anywhere.

00:09:18.889 --> 00:09:20.248
If you practice at something once a week,

00:09:20.248 --> 00:09:21.832
you're not going to get anywhere.

00:09:21.832 --> 00:09:23.154
Has to be daily.

00:09:23.154 --> 00:09:25.987
You have to find a time
to spend time daily

00:09:25.987 --> 00:09:28.813
at least 30 to 60
minutes every single day,

00:09:28.813 --> 00:09:31.171
on your business, on
achieving that ultimate goal

00:09:31.171 --> 00:09:33.584
to allow the momentum to build up.

00:09:33.584 --> 00:09:34.556
Most of you aren't hitting it

00:09:34.556 --> 00:09:36.178
because you're not consistent enough.

00:09:36.178 --> 00:09:39.698
(rhythmic music)

00:09:39.698 --> 00:09:41.962
#6 is your environment sucks.

00:09:41.962 --> 00:09:43.556
I touched on this a little bit earlier

00:09:43.556 --> 00:09:45.096
but the environment you're in matters.

00:09:45.096 --> 00:09:47.063
You are likely to be like your parents.

00:09:47.063 --> 00:09:48.396
You're likely to be like your friends.

00:09:48.396 --> 00:09:49.976
You're likely to be like
the people around you.

00:09:49.976 --> 00:09:51.786
It's really hard to break through.

00:09:51.786 --> 00:09:52.784
How do you break through?

00:09:52.784 --> 00:09:54.359
You start changing those things.

00:09:54.359 --> 00:09:55.610
And you may say well I don't know how

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:56.807
to hang out with different people,

00:09:56.807 --> 00:09:58.696
I don't know how to get access to them,

00:09:58.696 --> 00:10:01.090
if you're a face-to-face person
then go start to meet them,

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:03.436
go to events, go to
conferences, go to meet-ups,

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:06.166
go to the places where the
people who you want to be like,

00:10:06.166 --> 00:10:08.708
people who you want to
associate with are hanging out.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.294
'Cause it may not be in your backyard.

00:10:10.294 --> 00:10:11.966
It may not be on the
streets where you grew up.

00:10:11.966 --> 00:10:15.306
For me, it came from books initially

00:10:15.306 --> 00:10:16.744
and now it comes from videos.

00:10:16.744 --> 00:10:18.843
I feel like I'm hanging around Steve Jobs

00:10:18.843 --> 00:10:20.353
and Oprah Winfrey and the people

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:21.936
that I profile on my channel.

00:10:21.936 --> 00:10:24.439
I feel like every time
I watch their videos

00:10:24.439 --> 00:10:26.525
a little piece of them,
their thinking, their mindset

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:28.947
their way of being seeps into me,

00:10:28.947 --> 00:10:30.343
not to help me become like them

00:10:30.343 --> 00:10:32.565
but to help me become
a better version of me.

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:33.665
To help me play a bigger game,

00:10:33.665 --> 00:10:34.759
to help me have more confidence,

00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:36.559
to help me believe more.

00:10:36.559 --> 00:10:38.720
So those are the people
that I hang out with

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.711
on a consistent basis,

00:10:39.711 --> 00:10:41.824
because to be honest a lot of my friends,

00:10:41.824 --> 00:10:43.102
they're not pushing me.

00:10:43.102 --> 00:10:44.485
This happens for a lot of entrepreneurs.

00:10:44.485 --> 00:10:45.488
Your friends don't push you.

00:10:45.488 --> 00:10:46.798
Your friends respect you,

00:10:46.798 --> 00:10:48.699
your friends might be jealous of you,

00:10:48.699 --> 00:10:49.962
your friends might be saying

00:10:49.962 --> 00:10:51.181
what you're doing is really stupid,

00:10:51.181 --> 00:10:52.451
or they may be saying

00:10:52.451 --> 00:10:54.036
I wish I could do what you're doing.

00:10:54.036 --> 00:10:56.081
But who's telling you
you're doing a good job

00:10:56.081 --> 00:10:57.747
and you should be doing more.

00:10:57.747 --> 00:10:59.196
You should be playing way out here

00:10:59.196 --> 00:11:00.671
and you're playing this small game.

00:11:00.671 --> 00:11:03.564
A lot of us don't have that
because we don't have a boss.

00:11:03.564 --> 00:11:05.840
That's what a good boss
does, a good mentor does.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.466
They see the untapped potential in you

00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:09.437
and they help you get
to where you should be

00:11:09.437 --> 00:11:11.372
as opposed to where
you're limiting yourself.

00:11:11.372 --> 00:11:13.199
We don't have that a lot as entrepreneurs.

00:11:13.199 --> 00:11:14.610
We are our own boss.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.389
And yes, sometimes our
clients will push us

00:11:16.389 --> 00:11:17.500
and we'll have to make deadlines

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:18.640
and those kinds of things,

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:20.940
but in general, you know
you could be working harder.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.566
You know you haven't reached your ceiling,

00:11:22.566 --> 00:11:24.320
and you're not pushing
yourself through the discomfort

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.198
to go and reach that potential,

00:11:26.198 --> 00:11:27.876
because there's nobody out
there doing it for you.

00:11:27.876 --> 00:11:29.315
And so creating the environment

00:11:29.315 --> 00:11:30.925
that forces you to go out and do it,

00:11:30.925 --> 00:11:32.031
whether it's finding mentors,

00:11:32.031 --> 00:11:33.009
whether it's finding new friends,

00:11:33.009 --> 00:11:33.991
whether it's watching videos,

00:11:33.991 --> 00:11:35.046
whether it's listening to podcasts,

00:11:35.046 --> 00:11:36.887
whether it's consuming
books, whatever it is,

00:11:36.887 --> 00:11:39.320
look at the things that are around you,

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:40.260
your environment.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.576
What's on the wall in front of you,

00:11:42.576 --> 00:11:44.536
all of those things matter.

00:11:44.536 --> 00:11:45.992
You want to create an environment

00:11:45.992 --> 00:11:48.336
and a morning routine, especially rituals,

00:11:48.336 --> 00:11:51.174
that get you set up to do
something amazing today.

00:11:51.174 --> 00:11:53.024
We've all felt those moments of boldness

00:11:53.024 --> 00:11:54.766
where you felt unstoppable,

00:11:54.766 --> 00:11:56.347
where things would be amazing for you,

00:11:56.347 --> 00:11:59.404
and then the rest of
the week kind of sucked.

00:11:59.404 --> 00:12:01.016
So whatever you felt,
whatever was happening

00:12:01.016 --> 00:12:03.196
that got you all jazzed up and excited,

00:12:03.196 --> 00:12:05.123
whether you were watching an
interview or whatever it was,

00:12:05.123 --> 00:12:08.052
do that first thing
every day in the morning.

00:12:08.052 --> 00:12:09.377
And you'll need to find different sources

00:12:09.377 --> 00:12:11.255
because if all you're doing
is listening to the same video

00:12:11.255 --> 00:12:12.864
every day, you're going
to get bored of it.

00:12:12.864 --> 00:12:15.342
It may last for a week and then
it's going to lose its effect.

00:12:15.342 --> 00:12:16.608
But another video could help you

00:12:16.608 --> 00:12:17.624
and then another video could help you

00:12:17.624 --> 00:12:18.679
and another video could help you,

00:12:18.679 --> 00:12:20.380
which is why I started
the entspresso series

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.390
as a morning daily
thing to give you a shot

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:26.984
of ideas and inspiration
and wisdom and energy

00:12:26.984 --> 00:12:28.975
to go and do something
powerful and amazing

00:12:28.975 --> 00:12:31.411
in your business and your life today.

00:12:31.411 --> 00:12:33.100
Whether you watch the
entspresso series or not,

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.388
it doesn't matter to me,

00:12:34.388 --> 00:12:38.480
but find something that
makes you feel bold, inspired

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.830
and energetic and do that
first thing in the morning,

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.338
every single day to set
yourself up for success.

00:12:43.338 --> 00:12:46.088
(rhythmic music)

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.262
And the #7 reason why

00:12:48.262 --> 00:12:49.799
you have not achieved your ultimate goal

00:12:49.799 --> 00:12:51.536
is just a lack of self awareness.

00:12:51.536 --> 00:12:52.854
As I've been going through this process

00:12:52.854 --> 00:12:55.245
of helping people find their one word,

00:12:55.245 --> 00:12:58.304
I found how little people
actually know about themselves.

00:12:58.304 --> 00:13:00.759
How often people have sat in the industry

00:13:00.759 --> 00:13:03.901
just because that was the
practical thing to do.

00:13:03.901 --> 00:13:05.044
That's what their
parents wanted them to do

00:13:05.044 --> 00:13:06.233
or that's what they started university

00:13:06.233 --> 00:13:08.606
so they just kept along that path,

00:13:08.606 --> 00:13:09.823
and people have very little self-awareness

00:13:09.823 --> 00:13:11.728
for who they actually are,
and what do they value.

00:13:11.728 --> 00:13:14.343
If you don't know what you stand for,

00:13:14.343 --> 00:13:15.184
then you're just going to be subject

00:13:15.184 --> 00:13:16.678
to what other people stand for.

00:13:16.678 --> 00:13:18.396
Everybody has a plan for you.

00:13:18.396 --> 00:13:20.788
Your parents, your friends,
your colleagues, your customers,

00:13:20.788 --> 00:13:22.390
your suppliers, your investors.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:25.232
Everybody has a plan for you
or what you should be doing

00:13:25.232 --> 00:13:27.176
with your life that serves them.

00:13:27.176 --> 00:13:29.425
If you don't have a
great plan for yourself,

00:13:29.425 --> 00:13:31.127
you're just going to be
following everyone else's plan.

00:13:31.127 --> 00:13:33.232
You're never going to
get anywhere amazing.

00:13:33.232 --> 00:13:35.850
And so whether you believe
in finding the one word

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:37.785
and applying that to your
life and your business,

00:13:37.785 --> 00:13:40.153
or you go some other path,

00:13:40.153 --> 00:13:42.582
the idea of self-awareness
is really important.

00:13:42.582 --> 00:13:44.427
Why I find it so helpful is because

00:13:44.427 --> 00:13:47.936
I've realized that everything in my life

00:13:47.936 --> 00:13:50.167
has led up to where I am right now.

00:13:50.167 --> 00:13:52.641
And believe has always
played a part in it.

00:13:52.641 --> 00:13:53.675
Believe is my one word.

00:13:53.675 --> 00:13:55.611
It's always played a part of it.

00:13:55.611 --> 00:13:57.063
My favorite songs are about believe,

00:13:57.063 --> 00:13:58.439
my favorite movie is Seabiscuit,

00:13:58.439 --> 00:13:59.761
which is about believe,

00:13:59.761 --> 00:14:02.652
my parents taught me believe.

00:14:02.652 --> 00:14:04.400
Everything that's been good in my life,

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.846
came through the lens of believe.

00:14:05.846 --> 00:14:08.013
But it happened at random.

00:14:09.003 --> 00:14:12.415
These random moments of
greatness happened to me.

00:14:12.415 --> 00:14:14.196
When you understand what your one word is,

00:14:14.196 --> 00:14:16.309
when you have this self-awareness,

00:14:16.309 --> 00:14:18.488
then now you can take
that and start planning

00:14:18.488 --> 00:14:22.512
to let these good things
happen to you on purpose

00:14:22.512 --> 00:14:23.455
going forward,

00:14:23.455 --> 00:14:24.364
that you recognize them,

00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:25.769
that you start hanging
around the right people,

00:14:25.769 --> 00:14:27.964
that you start making the
powerful clear decisions,

00:14:27.964 --> 00:14:28.910
that you start getting results,

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.753
that you start achieving your goals.

00:14:30.753 --> 00:14:33.940
Otherwise you're going to
continue to live a random path

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.313
and you're going to continue to live up to

00:14:35.313 --> 00:14:37.752
other people's expectations
of what they want for you

00:14:37.752 --> 00:14:40.280
instead of the life that
you want for yourself.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.788
And so whether you're going with one word

00:14:41.788 --> 00:14:43.408
or you have another tool to help you,

00:14:43.408 --> 00:14:45.812
having a self awareness
to understand who you are,

00:14:45.812 --> 00:14:47.459
what you stand for, why you're here,

00:14:47.459 --> 00:14:49.706
what the powerful thing
is that you want to do,

00:14:49.706 --> 00:14:53.234
makes a huge difference for
your clarity, for your focus,

00:14:53.234 --> 00:14:55.279
and for your ability to follow
through and actually achieve

00:14:55.279 --> 00:14:56.812
in that ultimate goal for yourself.

00:14:56.812 --> 00:14:57.818
So those are my suggestions

00:14:57.818 --> 00:14:59.986
on the seven reasons why
you have not yet achieved

00:14:59.986 --> 00:15:01.117
your ultimate goal.

00:15:01.117 --> 00:15:02.868
I'd love to know what do you guys think,

00:15:02.868 --> 00:15:04.339
what was your favorite rule and why,

00:15:04.339 --> 00:15:05.478
did I miss an eight, nine, 10

00:15:05.478 --> 00:15:06.795
that you want to add to the list?

00:15:06.795 --> 00:15:07.931
Let me know down in the comments.

00:15:07.931 --> 00:15:10.041
Super curious to figure out
what you guys have to say.

00:15:10.041 --> 00:15:11.183
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:15:11.183 --> 00:15:14.913
to Jelena Ostrovska from
www.jelenaostrovska.com.

00:15:14.913 --> 00:15:15.873
Thank you so much, Jelena,

00:15:15.873 --> 00:15:18.247
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word.

00:15:18.247 --> 00:15:19.834
It really, really,
really means a lot to me,

00:15:19.834 --> 00:15:21.461
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:15:21.461 --> 00:15:22.657
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:22.657 --> 00:15:23.817
I believe in you.

00:15:23.817 --> 00:15:25.600
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:28.789
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:15:28.789 --> 00:15:30.019
I'll see you soon.

